{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/448782-sleepers","id":448782,"title":"Sleepers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-18T20:44:22-07:00","id":448782,"title":"Sleepers?","content":"I was wondering, what sorts of cool things have you cool guys done with sleeper agents? They don't get a whole lot of wordcount in <i>Demon</i>, but they're definitely presented as a threat of some sort. They're more or less normal mortal humans, which doesn't pose much of a direct threat to the Unchained, so I imagine most of the time their use is much more subtle. So what are some good, juicy story hooks for these dudes?<br /> <br /> The first that comes to mind to me is a sleeper agent being set up to sign a soul pact with a demon, thus allowing G-M agents to monitor the Unchained's activities once the honeypot is sprung.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T01:16:39-07:00","id":448925,"title":"","content":"A Demon PC has gained the Surveilled condition. While the agents of the God-Machine watch her cover, they take a mortal NPC associated with her cover, such as a loved one like a spouse or neighbor. The sleeper then maintains the watchful eye on the demon until the time is right and the Hunters come calling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T02:34:09-07:00","id":448954,"title":"","content":"It kind of violates merit sanctity, so see if the player is alright with it first, there's always the traditional having someone hunting and threatening to destroy an asset. The first one that came to mind was someone trying to murder the demon's cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T12:53:38-07:00","id":449618,"title":"","content":"Sanctity of Merits doesn't mean that all of a character's acquaintances, friends, or things are safe; it just means that if they're destroyed they make up those mechanical dots somewhere else. That said, I wouldn't have a player's human contacts be sleepers without good story justification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T16:01:03-07:00","id":449847,"title":"","content":"True Friend is the the specific method a player has to ensure that a supporting cast member, such as a spouse or the like, is theirs and should remain outside of the Storyteller's purview to damage on the whims of the story. Paranoia however is a large part of Demon and Sleepers are a huge way of illustrating a &quot;Trust No-One&quot; theme. Also keep in mind: Just because your Demon has a spouse doesn't mean that the Demon cares about the spouse. The spouse may be attached to their Cover, a Cover that they may have picked up recently wholesale via Soul Pact or by bartering away pieces of an unfaithful husband's life. The point of my suggestion is that a Sleeper can be <i>anyone</i> that could be taken by the agents of the God-Machine while the Demon isn't present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T13:37:20-07:00","id":450798,"title":"","content":"True Friend is a specific merit that declares that said person is protected. A friend isn't necessarily a True Friend.<br /> <br /> On topic, I know the example in the book isn't a stigmatic, but I'd guess that a reasonable amount are. Time spent in infrastructure is bound to leave a mark. Perhaps after a sleeper is activated they are more likely to manifest stigmata. I would assume that sleepers are left with the memories of what they did during activation; at the very least they're left with the consequences.<br /> <br /> A sleeper doesn't even necessarily have to be directly aimed at a PC to be an issue. A prominent politician or celebrity takes a wildly out of character action that sets the local scene ablaze. The fallout might brush up on the PC's interests; perhaps they try and contain the damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","user":"IceIX","date":". 03-20-2015, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T18:48:02-07:00","id":453526,"title":"","content":"Anyone can be a sleeper agent. A co-worker, a friend, the mother that bore you, anyone at all.<br /> Sleepers agents have no remorse, they only fulfill the mission.<br /> Sleepers agents are innocent, their will is suborned to the dictates of the G-m.<br /> Sleeper agents are doomed. One day, they\u2019re going to wake up in a room full of dead bodies and have no explanation as to why or how.<br /> <br /> Does any of this sound familiar? Hmmm? Okay, good, hold that thought.<br /> My master class lesson in using sleepers is this: make your players empathize with sleepers. If you can, do this from the perspective of the characters with the uncomfortable similarities between how the G-m treats humans and angels alike, and also from the perspective of the players themselves. Get them to see themselves in someone who can have their life upended at any time.<br /> <br /> At very least they should should hesitate before they pull the trigger.<br /> <br /> The best use of a sleeper agent in my chronicle was after a player stopped fearing compromise checks after his Wits+ Manipulation hit critical mass. When he finally failed a roll, I told him not to take a dot of his cover. The next day a co-worker walked into the school where he worked\u2026 and started shooting.<br /> <br /> <i>Then</i> I took off the dot of cover, handed him the Surveilled condition and told him to have fun keeping the students alive without blowing his Cover. In the aftermath the player learned he had triggered his co-workers programming through negligent disregard of his cover. She was now looking at a life sentence in prison, and it was his fault.<br /> <br /> Edit: I neglected to mention the best part. Earlier in the Chronicle, the player had lovingly described the type of gun his character used, complete with modifications. To rub salt in the wound, I made sure the sleeper was using that <i>exact</i> type of weapon, complete with the modifications when she began her rampage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 03-24-2015, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}